WEBVTT

00:04.440 --> 00:06.320
The AUZA Reactor...

00:06.400 --> 00:09.839
<i>It produces 2.2 million
kilowatts per second.</i>

00:09.919 --> 00:11.880
<i>That's high power, the equivalent of one
and a half nuclear power plants.</i>

00:12.759 --> 00:14.839
<i>Our newly-discovered
fuel source, cuborium,</i>

00:14.919 --> 00:18.600
<i>can produce unlimited heat
via fusion reaction.</i>

00:19.399 --> 00:21.600
It's clean and low-cost.

00:22.079 --> 00:24.480
<i>The price of energy
in AUZA City is unprecedented.</i>

00:25.120 --> 00:28.600
<i>Our customers pay 80% less than
anywhere else in the world.</i>

00:30.079 --> 00:32.280
<i>Reinventing the world
of tomorrow...</i>

00:32.359 --> 00:33.759
the AUZA Reactor.

00:35.960 --> 00:37.880
So what do you think, Mr. Secretary?

00:38.880 --> 00:41.240
It goes without saying, but we could
build even more power plants

00:41.320 --> 00:43.399
with the backing of
the Department of Energy.

00:44.159 --> 00:45.359
We can't fast-track this.

00:45.960 --> 00:47.679
There are fisheries and
environmental groups strongly

00:47.759 --> 00:50.759
opposed to any facilities
being built along the coast.

00:52.000 --> 00:54.439
So even if the department
were to grant approval...

00:54.920 --> 00:57.000
I wish you wouldn't sell us so short.

00:57.799 --> 01:01.560
We at AUZA actually formed
an advisory committee just the other day,

01:02.039 --> 01:05.879
and the fine folks who agreed to join it
are everyone listed here.

01:09.920 --> 01:10.879
What? That's impossible.

01:11.840 --> 01:14.519
Animosity is really just
another form of keen interest,

01:15.159 --> 01:18.480
so people getting to reverse their
positions is easier than you think.

01:19.319 --> 01:21.840
There's no way these people
would ever agree to this.

01:22.760 --> 01:23.680
Whoopsie-daisy.

01:24.439 --> 01:26.519
Just how much did you
bite them off for?

01:26.599 --> 01:27.519
Buy-off.

01:29.640 --> 01:33.680
Rushing development like this
will always lead to failure.

01:35.120 --> 01:37.480
We would never resort
to such a childish game.

01:38.519 --> 01:41.920
Like I said earlier,
don't sell us so short.

01:45.599 --> 01:49.200
<i>Part of Yamaji's plan is letting AUZA
use his forces as their muscle.</i>

01:50.640 --> 01:52.560
They plan on seizing
all energy infrastructure

01:52.959 --> 01:56.439
and then assume control
of each country from the inside.

01:57.000 --> 01:58.200
After I became one
of their lieutenants,

01:58.680 --> 02:02.159
I learned that the organization
was no more than AUZA's puppet.

02:03.280 --> 02:06.359
He and the others no longer had honor
or respect for the ninja way.

02:06.799 --> 02:08.639
That's why I feel
this was my destiny.

02:09.400 --> 02:13.439
All the time I spent observing them was
so that I could ultimately assist you.

03:47.360 --> 03:49.960
Why'd you have to go
and tell me all that stuff?

03:50.599 --> 03:54.400
I mean, ninjas? Doesn't get
more dangerous than that.

03:54.479 --> 03:56.680
Aw, hell, dude,
we're gonna be so screwed.

03:57.000 --> 03:58.919
We don't have time
for your freak-out, man.

03:59.400 --> 04:01.639
This place isn't safe.
They could attack us at any--

04:01.719 --> 04:04.759
And whose fault is that?
You got me into this mess.

04:05.680 --> 04:07.680
Listen, do you really think
you'd have been

04:07.759 --> 04:09.680
any safer hacking away alone
in your nerd cave?

04:10.680 --> 04:11.879
That's what happens

04:11.960 --> 04:13.719
when you start snooping around and
messing with these guys.

04:14.400 --> 04:17.600
And once you stuck your neck out, then
all you can do is keep pressing on.

04:19.959 --> 04:20.879
So dig deep.

04:21.560 --> 04:23.800
Remember your grudge
and help me bring him down.

04:27.040 --> 04:28.920
Okay. I'm in.
But are you going to protect me?

04:29.600 --> 04:32.360
Of course I'll protect you. But there's
something we're going to need first.

04:32.439 --> 04:33.759
I need a computer, dude.

04:35.439 --> 04:38.600
Hey, there was a name you
recognized on that list, right?

04:39.199 --> 04:41.920
Who is that Emma person?

04:49.959 --> 04:54.279
Ah, geez. We got to go through all this
crap because of some damn terrorist?

05:09.639 --> 05:10.759
Here we go.

05:23.480 --> 05:25.040
What the hell?

05:34.639 --> 05:36.439
- Mobilize the drones.
- We can't.

05:36.839 --> 05:38.480
The entire system is down.

05:46.959 --> 05:48.279
Where's Yamaji now?

05:49.000 --> 05:52.879
I don't know, but I'm positive that he
must be putting his plans into motion.

05:53.839 --> 05:55.360
Our actions have left him
with no other choice.

05:56.600 --> 05:58.519
We should make our next move
as soon as possible.

05:59.519 --> 06:01.079
We'll head for this
unfinished power plant

06:01.600 --> 06:04.279
and use the energy there
to supercharge your gusoku gear.

06:04.360 --> 06:06.839
There should be some portable
energy tanks that we can take.

06:07.920 --> 06:09.560
- Operational test?
- Yeah.

06:10.120 --> 06:11.720
It's planned for tomorrow.

06:12.160 --> 06:14.079
My intel says that
their lieutenants will be there

06:14.720 --> 06:17.240
to make sure that the gear
will react properly.

06:18.600 --> 06:22.639
That's great. I can force them
to cough up Yamaji's location.

06:23.560 --> 06:25.680
You were in ideal form
during that last battle.

06:26.199 --> 06:27.759
Remember the sensation
you felt then?

06:28.360 --> 06:29.720
The less distracted you are,

06:30.199 --> 06:32.560
the smoother the gusoku gear
will operate.

06:33.680 --> 06:35.480
You must tame your rage.

06:39.079 --> 06:40.279
My rage is not...

06:41.720 --> 06:43.560
something that I can suppress easily.

06:59.680 --> 07:03.439
<i>Be as cold as fire
and as hot as ice.</i>

07:05.000 --> 07:10.000
<i>Mari used to tell me her
dream for you was to... live on.</i>

07:15.120 --> 07:17.120
The gusoku gears' performance in battle

07:17.639 --> 07:20.639
results from his heart and willpower.

07:23.360 --> 07:24.680
But nevertheless...

07:28.040 --> 07:31.160
I will be the one to protect him.

08:06.199 --> 08:08.160
Are you impressed,
Mrs. Defense Secretary?

08:08.879 --> 08:12.120
It only lasts about five minutes
with the current battery system.

08:12.600 --> 08:14.560
But when the suit is utilized
at maximum strength,

08:15.199 --> 08:17.839
these are the kind of results
that it can produce.

08:19.199 --> 08:20.199
I see now.

08:20.959 --> 08:22.399
Ninjas can be very threatening.

08:28.040 --> 08:31.560
<i>Attention. We are now starting
the operations test as planned.</i>

08:32.000 --> 08:34.279
3, 2, 1.

08:44.919 --> 08:45.879
The test worked.

08:54.399 --> 08:56.559
I've managed to secure
a portable energy tank.

08:57.200 --> 08:59.120
I'm heading your way now.

09:02.240 --> 09:05.000
I've been looking for you, Judas.

09:07.519 --> 09:08.759
You will not escape.

09:23.639 --> 09:26.679
Interesting.
The warrior type, huh?

09:29.320 --> 09:31.639
I've always wanted to bust it up
with an adversary like you.

09:32.840 --> 09:34.840
And in the face of a true warrior,

09:34.919 --> 09:37.639
I would neither run nor hide
in the shadows like a rat.

09:38.080 --> 09:41.279
So let's settle this fair and square.
I know exactly what you're after.

09:43.039 --> 09:44.960
You want to know
where the boss is.

09:45.679 --> 09:47.200
I will tell you
if you can defeat me.

09:47.960 --> 09:52.360
This is no game.
I'm just a beautiful human being

09:52.840 --> 09:57.120
who doesn't want to stain his reputation
with any spite born out of battle.

09:58.240 --> 09:59.440
Sounds like a trap to me.

10:00.240 --> 10:01.440
It doesn't matter.

10:01.840 --> 10:04.600
The fact remains we can't win
unless we face him head-on.

10:05.600 --> 10:06.600
Come, now.

10:07.120 --> 10:09.960
Let's make this a graceful battle.

10:29.000 --> 10:31.000
<i>The enemy must have
some plan up their sleeve.</i>

10:31.360 --> 10:34.120
<i>So how can we tip the scales
in our favor before they use it on us?</i>

10:35.519 --> 10:37.200
The Reactor system.

10:40.519 --> 10:43.879
<i>That'll work. If I just shut down
their ability to resupply wirelessly...</i>

12:24.919 --> 12:28.639
The system is down now.
That cuts off our energy supply.

12:29.759 --> 12:33.720
All I need to do is call my crew,
and you two would be dead meat.

12:34.840 --> 12:38.559
But I don't play like that when
I'm in battle against a true warrior.

12:40.000 --> 12:45.240
The next time we meet, let there
be no interruptions, only elegance.

12:53.440 --> 12:56.519
- I'd like to ask you something.
- What do you want to know?

12:57.639 --> 12:59.600
Why do you go out of your way
to protect me?

13:02.000 --> 13:05.200
I know you said you wanted
to uphold Mari's wish, but...

13:05.960 --> 13:07.919
it's not as if she asked you
to, right?

13:08.919 --> 13:11.320
Yes. You're right.
I'm just being selfish.

13:12.720 --> 13:14.879
It's part of a promise
that I made with myself,

13:15.799 --> 13:18.159
to follow through
with everything, no matter what.

13:18.799 --> 13:22.000
That's what my heart settled on
after Mari died.

13:23.279 --> 13:24.759
I don't expect you to understand,

13:25.600 --> 13:28.879
because it's something personal that I
have to accomplish for myself.

13:30.080 --> 13:32.480
<i>Mari used to tell me her dream
for you was to...</i>

13:33.480 --> 13:34.559
live on.

13:38.320 --> 13:39.759
Accomplish for yourself, huh?

13:44.360 --> 13:46.759
It's my computer.
Someone's booted it up.

13:47.399 --> 13:48.639
Is it the organization?

13:48.720 --> 13:50.720
That would be
the most natural conclusion.

13:52.639 --> 13:53.759
Or maybe...

13:57.440 --> 14:00.120
Thank God we were able
to take it without any hassle.

14:00.200 --> 14:02.440
Gotta hand it to you.
That FBI badge is hella useful.

14:03.000 --> 14:03.919
It can be.

14:04.240 --> 14:06.200
How long do you think
you can keep using it?

14:06.279 --> 14:07.679
You can't go back there, right?

14:08.519 --> 14:10.519
Being with the FBI isn't important.

14:12.320 --> 14:15.799
When I'm all said and done, protecting
innocent citizens is a job I gave myself.

14:17.480 --> 14:21.480
No luck. I can't crack this.
The encryption is just way too strong.

14:22.559 --> 14:24.879
Come on. Don't you geeks
love this kind of stuff?

14:25.960 --> 14:29.480
Yeah, but tech skills at this level,
only a genius could pull this stuff off.

14:30.080 --> 14:31.080
It's a red flag, dude.

14:31.159 --> 14:33.159
This Emma person must be
some kind of big-shot.

14:33.799 --> 14:34.840
You might be right.

14:36.159 --> 14:39.159
Hey, man. Come on,
you gotta watch the road.

14:41.639 --> 14:44.279
Why'd the car's radio suddenly turn on?

14:45.759 --> 14:46.960
This song...

14:49.600 --> 14:53.039
<i>Hey, rookie, can you guess
why I asked you here?</i>

14:53.840 --> 14:56.159
- No.
- To chew you out, obviously.

14:56.840 --> 14:58.799
You got to stop acting
on your own so damn much.

14:59.360 --> 15:00.480
I know you're eager about the job,

15:01.279 --> 15:02.919
but you've been pulling
this crap ever since training.

15:03.000 --> 15:04.919
I act on my own
because I'm a professional.

15:06.000 --> 15:09.279
I know there are times when a delay in
judgment can lead to costly mistakes.

15:09.799 --> 15:10.960
That's not the point here.

15:11.919 --> 15:14.519
What I'm trying to say is that
you lack faith in your friends.

15:15.000 --> 15:17.240
- That is so not true.
- It is.

15:17.320 --> 15:18.960
- Is not.
- Is so.

15:25.799 --> 15:29.279
Shit. Do you even realize how long
I've been an investigator?

15:31.679 --> 15:33.600
Just let me have
your back, okay?

15:34.000 --> 15:36.799
In this business, your partner
is as good as family.

15:41.279 --> 15:43.360
- What's the matter?
- It's nothing.

15:44.279 --> 15:46.600
We're not family, though.
You're a colleague.

15:47.159 --> 15:50.159
What the hell is your problem?

15:50.720 --> 15:52.759
Why are you trying to go
and kill my good mood?

15:54.000 --> 15:56.840
This is so painful.
It's just not my style.

15:57.399 --> 15:58.679
What?!

15:58.759 --> 16:00.720
Come on!
The ambiance in here is perfect.

16:01.639 --> 16:03.360
Even the song choice
is totally on point.

16:37.279 --> 16:38.480
Yeah!

16:57.440 --> 17:01.080
Holy crap! They're coming for us!

17:01.159 --> 17:02.240
Don't jump the gun.

17:05.839 --> 17:06.880
Wait for my signal.

17:15.799 --> 17:16.880
It's you?

17:23.359 --> 17:24.480
I see how it is.

17:24.559 --> 17:26.759
To think you were a ninja
the whole damn time.

17:26.839 --> 17:29.519
- Are you in cahoots with the FBI?
- No.

17:30.319 --> 17:32.799
Not a single person at the FBI
knows the truth.

17:33.400 --> 17:35.119
I was simply just following orders.

17:35.200 --> 17:36.559
So you're a ninja and a spy, then?

17:38.559 --> 17:40.880
What I did was inexcusable, and
an apology won't help that now.

17:41.359 --> 17:43.680
You make it sound like you
don't even want to say you're sorry.

17:45.160 --> 17:46.359
That sounds about right.

17:46.960 --> 17:50.720
Well, good for you, but that sure as hell
doesn't sit right with me.

17:51.400 --> 17:52.839
You put me on this guy's trail
just to lead me further

17:53.359 --> 17:55.920
from the truth, isn't that right?

17:57.960 --> 18:00.400
This is worse than just
stabbing me in the back.

18:00.480 --> 18:02.720
What you did, it goes against...

18:07.440 --> 18:09.720
Sorry. I need some time alone.

18:10.359 --> 18:11.880
I gotta process all this shit.

18:15.079 --> 18:17.680
Son of a...

18:18.599 --> 18:19.880
Damn it!

18:26.559 --> 18:29.079
I'm sorry for keeping
the truth from you.

18:32.160 --> 18:35.279
It was a duty you swore
to uphold until the end, right?

18:38.960 --> 18:42.160
- What's this?
- This is my sworn duty.

18:43.119 --> 18:45.640
My daughter died in an accident,
and I couldn't save her.

18:46.319 --> 18:47.799
Those are the words
she left behind.

18:49.279 --> 18:52.319
It's something that nags at me,
like a curse I can't break.

18:53.079 --> 18:55.920
I'm always thinking,
"I got to do this.

18:57.160 --> 18:58.799
I got to see it through."

19:00.319 --> 19:03.000
My heart feels bound to it.

19:04.359 --> 19:06.079
And if experience
has taught me anything,

19:07.039 --> 19:08.680
it's that all humans
are like this.

19:11.039 --> 19:12.839
Everybody goes through life
burdened by some curse.

19:13.279 --> 19:14.720
Now I know the same
is true of you.

19:16.319 --> 19:17.720
Besides, I wasn't pissed off

19:17.799 --> 19:19.640
by the fact that you were
hiding things from me.

19:24.119 --> 19:26.359
I told you before.
Come on, let me have your back.

19:26.440 --> 19:27.680
This is a lovely drawing.

19:28.240 --> 19:29.519
It may seem like a curse
to you now,

19:29.599 --> 19:31.240
but there might come
a time down the road

19:32.759 --> 19:34.000
when it proves to be useful.

19:34.079 --> 19:35.880
Care for a drink,
just like old times?

19:41.079 --> 19:42.200
Ah, shit!

19:46.359 --> 19:48.680
AUZA is building more and more
of these power plants in a bid

19:48.759 --> 19:50.880
to take control of this
country's energy infrastructure.

19:51.200 --> 19:54.000
And the ninjas are the force
they use to accomplish that?

19:54.519 --> 19:55.759
No way.

19:55.839 --> 19:58.279
When the hell did they develop
this kind of technology?

19:58.599 --> 19:59.839
It's totally unbelievable.

20:00.279 --> 20:03.400
This footage here,
it would never pass as evidence.

20:03.880 --> 20:06.160
It would quickly
be passed off as fake.

20:06.880 --> 20:11.119
However, we cannot afford
to just sit around here

20:11.559 --> 20:13.119
and twiddle our thumbs.

20:13.200 --> 20:15.960
Letting their plans come to fruition will
mean the end of this country.

20:16.039 --> 20:17.759
Those frigging bastards.

20:19.920 --> 20:23.200
In any case, we'd like you
to either cover up this incident

20:23.279 --> 20:24.960
or make a public announcement

20:25.039 --> 20:27.559
that will put the minds
of our citizens at ease.

20:28.119 --> 20:30.799
Okay, okay. It's not a problem.

20:31.319 --> 20:35.000
The trust you have placed in us
can endure a small hiccup like this.

20:43.000 --> 20:47.920
Revised and Synchronized by
FAST TITLES MEDIA
